  "notes": "Per the 2026-2027 Texas A&M University undergraduate catalog: Physics — Physics and Mathematics Teaching Track (BS). Prerequisites are not listed in the catalog's plan of study grid; consult course descriptions.\nCatalog footnotes:\n[grid1 fn1] A Physics major must complete the foundation courses ( ASTR 102 , PHYS 101 , PHYS 150 , PHYS 206 / PHYS 226 , PHYS 207 / PHYS 227 , PHYS 221 , PHYS 309 , PHYS 331 , MATH 171 , MATH 172 , MATH 221 , MATH 308 ) with a grade of C or better and have a 2.0 cumulative GPA before taking non-foundation upper-level physics courses.\n[grid1 fn2] Any course in this category from the approved University Core Curriculum list of courses.\n[grid1 fn3] INST 222 is an approved Social and Behavioral Science and Cultural Discourse class.\n[grid1 fn4] PHYS 327 is an approved University Writing course.\n[grid1 fn5] PHYS 328 is an approved University Communication course.\n[grid1 fn6] Students must apply, and be admitted, to aggieTEACH, before beginning this class. Students are required to have 2.75 overall GPA and a 2.5 GPA in content areas.\n[grid1 fn7] Electives should be chosen in consultation with the student's advisor. Electives may be selected from any 100-499 course not used elsewhere, except ENGL 103 ; MATH 100-148, 165-166, 365-366; PHYS 201 , PHYS 202\n[grid1 fn8] Any upper-division course in geo/life/physical sciences, mathematics/statistics or engineering (except 485/491). Note: students seeking secondary certification through this degree must take MATH 403 for this elective.",
